sensor-bme680 (2.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * "mock" is a table of values passed to the library rather than hand-built
    JSON, so it cannot drift from the real output format
  * "enable" now enables I2C, by adding dtparam=i2c_arm=on to the Pi boot
    config, instead of printing a note telling the user to run raspi-config.
    The kernel exposes no I2C bus until that is set, so a driver whose "enable"
    did nothing left the sensor unusable by its own instructions. Running it
    twice is safe: the second run reports that it is already enabled
  * Build the output array with the library's JSON array builder instead of
    realloc and strcat, which was repeated once per measurement. The four
    near-identical blocks are now one call each
  * Use the library's WS_UNIT_* constants rather than unit string literals
  * Config parsing moves to the library's ws_config_iter_* and the common
    fields to an embedded ws_sensor_config_base_t, leaving i2c_addr as the only
    field this driver declares and parses for itself
  * No longer crashes when no sensor_id can be determined. A config entry
    without sensor_id on a host whose /proc/cpuinfo has no Serial line (a
    non-Pi I2C host) left sensor_id NULL, which was then passed to strlen().
    The reading is now emitted with a null sensor_id instead
  * The four per-measurement id allocations are no longer unchecked, and the
    duplicated size arithmetic is now in one helper
  * "mock" no longer prints "(null)_temperature" where the host has no Pi
    serial; it falls back to a fixed id, mock being the command meant to work
    without the hardware
  * Rebuild against libwildlifesystems 1.3.0, so "{{node}}" in a sensor's
    location resolves to the node's own coordinates from /etc/geolocation
    instead of being emitted as an unresolved token
  * Require libwildlifesystems-dev (>= 1.3.0). The library is static, so the
    behaviour above is fixed at build time: a binary built against 1.2.0 would
    satisfy the old pin and silently emit unresolved tokens under the same
    package version

 -- Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0100

sensor-bme680 (2.2.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Zero-initialise default_config. It sets every field explicitly except
    location, which was left reading uninitialised stack memory on nodes with
    no config file; a garbage source of WS_LOC_EXPLICIT would have emitted a
    GeoJSON Point built from uninitialised coordinates

 -- Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0100

sensor-bme680 (2.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Report device "bme680" and the sensor's configured location
  * Support "location" in /etc/ws/sensors/bme680.json
  * Use ws_json_object_end for config object bounds, so a config entry may
    contain nested objects
  * Rebuild against libwildlifesystems 1.2.0
  * Declare libwildlifesystems-dev (>= 1.2.0) in Build-Depends and
    sensor-control (>= 1.3.0) in Depends. Neither was declared at all,
    though the binary links -lwildlifesystems and runs sc-prototype

 -- Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0100

